{"name":"Great White","hex":"#bdbdc6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"great white","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Ellipsis of great white shark."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/great_white"}],"entries":[{"title":"Great white shark","blocks":[{"text":"The great white shark, also known as the white shark, white pointer, or great white, is a large shark. It is closely related to the mako sharks, the porbeagle, and the salmon shark. It is a robustly built species with a grayish upperside and a white underside. The white shark is one of the largest living shark and fish species, though it is still smaller than the whale shark and basking shark. It has about 300 triangular, serrated teeth that are continuously replaced. Its massive, fatty liver can reach over a quarter of its body weight, providing buoyancy and storing energy. The species is partially warm-blooded, an adaptation that allows it to remain active in colder waters."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/White_shark.jpg/330px-White_shark.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_white_shark","wikidata":"Q129026"},{"title":"Great egret","blocks":[{"text":"The great egret, also known as the common egret, large egret, great white egret, or great white heron, is a large, widely distributed egret. The four subspecies are found in Asia, Africa, the Americas, and southern Europe. Recently, it has also been spreading to more northern areas of Europe. Distributed across most of the tropical and warmer temperate regions of the world, it builds tree nests in colonies close to water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Great_Egret_%28Ardea_alba%29_in_Breeding_Plumage%2C_Cape_May_County%2C_New_Jersey%2C_USA_%28cropped%29.png/330px-Great_Egret_%28Ardea_alba%29_in_Breeding_Plumage%2C_Cape_May_County%2C_New_Jersey%2C_USA_%28cropped%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_egret","wikidata":"Q130730"},{"title":"Great White","blocks":[{"text":"Great White is an American hard rock band formed in Los Angeles in 1977. The band is named after both the shark with the same name, and guitarist Mark Kendall's former stage nickname. In August 2008, the band estimated they had sold around eight million records worldwide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Great_White_at_the_Moondance_Jam.jpg/330px-Great_White_at_the_Moondance_Jam.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_White","wikidata":"Q1330850"},{"title":"Great White (1981 film)","blocks":[{"text":"The Last Shark is a 1981 Italian horror film directed by Enzo G. Castellari, having originally been assigned to Ruggero Deodato. \nIn the film James Franciscus and Vic Morrow attempt to save hundreds of swimmers in a coastal resort after a large great white shark starts terrorizing the area and eating tourists."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6a/L%27ultim-squalo-italian-filmposter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_White_(1981_film)","wikidata":"Q1620043"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Evolution_of_the_great_white_shark.jpg/500px-Evolution_of_the_great_white_shark.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Evolution_of_the_great_white_shark.jpg/1280px-Evolution_of_the_great_white_shark.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Evolution_of_the_great_white_shark.jpg/500px-Evolution_of_the_great_white_shark.jpg?utm_source=en.wiki